From: Antonio Terceiro <terceiro@debian.org>
Date: Sat, 20 Aug 2022 17:58:57 -0300
Subject: gemspec, spec_helper: drop require_relative to lib/ directory

This allows the test suite to run against the installed package. I tried
to submit this upstream but was rejected.

Link: https://github.com/rack/rack-test/pull/319
Forwarded: not-needed
---
 rack-test.gemspec   | 3 ++-
 spec/spec_helper.rb | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rack-test.gemspec b/rack-test.gemspec
index 649caf3..8c1139b 100644
--- a/rack-test.gemspec
+++ b/rack-test.gemspec
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
-require_relative 'lib/rack/test/version'
+$:.unshift(File.expand_path("lib", File.dirname(__FILE__)))
+require 'rack/test/version'
 
 Gem::Specification.new do |s|
   s.name = 'rack-test'
diff --git a/spec/spec_helper.rb b/spec/spec_helper.rb
index 8c527c7..ac231da 100644
--- a/spec/spec_helper.rb
+++ b/spec/spec_helper.rb
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ ENV['MT_NO_PLUGINS'] = '1' # Work around stupid autoloading of plugins
 gem 'minitest'
 require 'minitest/global_expectations/autorun'
 
-require_relative '../lib/rack/test'
+require 'rack/test'
 require_relative 'fixtures/fake_app'
 
 class Minitest::Spec
